                        ],
                        "form": "пе́сеннике"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9e6540c5-3cbf-48c4-a503-3602870df25c",
                        "entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "пе́сенниках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cddcf5a1-a390-33e1-a037-d38603f6d403",
                        "entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "певец, исполнитель песен, любитель или умелец петь"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cd5b5678-d4e2-4a4a-a1c3-6d76b282f10e",
                                "sense_id": "cddcf5a1-a390-33e1-a037-d38603f6d403",
                                "text": "Обыкновенно впереди эскадрона едут песенники и поют почти во весь переход; не думаю, чтоб им это было очень весело; даже и по доброй воле наскучило бы петь целый день, а поневоле и подавно."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "20314a31-fea8-4d02-a0c0-b4d736c32c88",
                                "sense_id": "cddcf5a1-a390-33e1-a037-d38603f6d403",
                                "text": "Русская песня начинается запевалой, самым голосистым песенником изо всех."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60f79be7-53f5-3397-a9ca-64c90de4787f",
                        "entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "композитор или поэт, чьё творчество связано с написанием песен"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef72f864-1fb5-4528-898b-cf4b855f1c75",
                                "sense_id": "60f79be7-53f5-3397-a9ca-64c90de4787f",
                                "text": "Мне трудно сейчас сказать, отчего творческая судьба Бабаджаняна сложилась так, а не иначе. Массовому слушателю он известен как блистательный песенник, знатокам серьёзной музыки ― как автор академических произведений."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f6810dac-a090-3779-86e2-f5616a633fca",
                        "entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "сборник песен"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b4cda5a9-46ad-4c47-af13-e9f74e52d409",
                                "sense_id": "f6810dac-a090-3779-86e2-f5616a633fca",
                                "text": "Подарите мне новейший песенник! Такой, знаете, толстый, с картинкой на обложке, ― хоровод девицы водят."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c844f239-56ff-42d1-aea7-ab867e77e8fc",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "source_sense_description": "исполнитель песен",
                        "target_lang_word": "songster",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "songster",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acc6d186-253c-36b4-aa4e-4206df8a2d1d",
                                        "entry_id": "34742c92-0afd-309b-ab9b-5604be62d117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who sings songs, especially as a profession; a male singer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c5855295-e845-3118-af14-417ce0074cce",
                                        "entry_id": "34742c92-0afd-309b-ab9b-5604be62d117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An adult chorister in the Salvation Army."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "daafcced-70c1-4a9c-b1aa-f45fd4c389e1",
                                                "sense_id": "c5855295-e845-3118-af14-417ce0074cce",
                                                "text": "A member of a Salvation Army family, she had been a songster accompanying the band around the streets of Chelmsford where she lived with her parents."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66a2f95e-43e5-4771-8a9f-35bacd9753ae",
                                                "sense_id": "c5855295-e845-3118-af14-417ce0074cce",
                                                "text": "On a later occasion he returned to the theme of keeping the individuality of Salvation Army music, and resisting the temptation for songster brigades to imitate chapel and mission choirs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b315bdd-5605-3d66-9bbd-93682054e292",
                                        "entry_id": "34742c92-0afd-309b-ab9b-5604be62d117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A male songbird."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e74f6cf-e54b-4bcb-a213-5badb5d031fa",
                                                "sense_id": "6b315bdd-5605-3d66-9bbd-93682054e292",
                                                "text": "The woodcock, the snipe, and other nocturnal birds were all gone to rest; but the merry songsters of the wood now filled the air with their jubilee; the nutcracker began his monotonous clattering, the chaffinches and the wrens sang high in the sky, the blackcock scolded and blustered loudly, the thrush sang his mocking songs and libellous ditties about everybody, but became occasionally a little sentimental and warbled gently and bashfully some tender stanzas."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "005b1999-54d5-3f69-9a34-5b07ad1a70d0",
                                        "entry_id": "34742c92-0afd-309b-ab9b-5604be62d117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who writes songs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "454112f9-8f4e-3760-b341-8e8532cd6881",
                                        "entry_id": "34742c92-0afd-309b-ab9b-5604be62d117",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A book of songs; songbook."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53814412-ad56-4529-8756-c5d81c8b5233",
                                                "sense_id": "454112f9-8f4e-3760-b341-8e8532cd6881",
                                                "text": "Because the Jew was often compelled to sing and dance to a fixed Mah Yafit melody at the wild orgies of the paritzim (wealthy Polish landowners), many deliberately discontinued singing Mah Yafit, thus causing the text to be removed from numerous Siddurim and songsters in the early 1900s."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "458b7422-4246-46a2-a04d-cc287a5fb7a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "source_sense_description": "автор песен",
                        "target_lang_word": "songwriter",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "songwriter",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ef0c1789-5244-39ac-89ce-db1fce6bc9a7",
                                        "entry_id": "30747e59-7886-30dc-9b63-2b9511ce5d02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A musician who composes songs; especially writing the song's lyrics and/or creating a melody or a tune for the song."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62354c8b-b778-454f-bbe0-f34fd5995df0",
                                                "sense_id": "ef0c1789-5244-39ac-89ce-db1fce6bc9a7",
                                                "text": "We are now collaborating with a famous songwriter."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ddf3f9cb-5d10-4e6c-8f5d-e46fc5e079e4",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
                        "source_sense_description": "сборник песен",
                        "target_lang_word": "songbook",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "songbook",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                        "entry_id": "93e3668a-28fa-3dbb-8e60-7830aa36c6bd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A book containing songs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c7a8953-ba69-4a27-92fe-d71180832bf9",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "Some of the young folks asked Mrs. Long could they have a sing at her home that Sunday afternoon; she readily agreed, telling them to come early, bring their songbooks, and have a good sing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "790b76f4-262d-4aeb-acea-33d83b0c718e",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "In uncritical homage to the heyday of Hollywood musicals, Branagh sets the action in a kind of soundstagey Oxbridge (wittily designed by Tim Harvey) and at crucial moments has his cast spin on their heels and croon American songbook standards by Porter, Kern, Gershwin and company instead of launching into sonnets and masques."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80343da1-04a2-427f-b264-21def2ba598d",
                                                "sense_id": "d733f541-e3be-3efe-8bac-2e4bab83bea0",
                                                "text": "Wondering how else he passed his time, Winifred surveyed the room again, this time without regard for the monetary value of the things she saw. A box of lutestrings. Five songbooks. But no lute."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7dabd7fa-d482-4c4a-ab23-1fe229bc7d1e",
                        "source_entry_id": "ba3c941e-47e1-3bb7-8491-5eb8a1e1a63f",
